  "issues": [
    "The job's output and error streams are directed to files within an `output/` subdirectory (e.g., `#FLUX --output=output/slurm_{id}.out`). However, the script itself does not create this top-level directory. If the `output/` directory does not exist in the submission path when the job starts, the job will fail immediately because it cannot open its log files. A `mkdir -p output` command should be added at the beginning of the script.",
    "The script calculates the memory available for the application as one-quarter of the total allocated memory (`bytes_of_memory=$((${FLUX_JOB_MEM_PER_NODE}*1024 / 4))`). While providing a memory buffer is common practice, reducing the available memory to 25% of the requested 192GB is a very large reduction and may lead to significant underutilization of memory resources or cause the application to perform poorly if it is memory-bound. This calculation should be reviewed to ensure it is intentional."
  ]
}
